@@ -23,4 +23,10 @@ Resolve the immutable source revision before rendering. The cache key includes c
 
 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The cache uses a 2Q eviction policy. Two queues separate first-use entries (A1) from entries that have been reused at least once (Am). New entries start in A1; a hit in A1 promotes the entry to Am, while a hit in Am updates recency within Am. Eviction removes from A1 first, protecting reused comparison sheets from sequential screening scans. Queue size split between A1 and Am is a tunable parameter. Bookkeeping is private to the preview worker and does not change the external API, render queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings. Extra bookkeeping is acceptable to preserve the working set. LRU is vulnerable to scan eviction; frequency with aging adds counter maintenance and can retain stale favorites too long. |
